using this formula:
\begin{align}
\mathcal G = \frac{16\omega_m^2t}{\gamma^3\Gamma}
\int_{-\infty}^{\infty} \frac{d\Omega}{2\pi}\Bk{\Omega^2 -\bk{g^{-2}-1+\Gamma^2/4}}^2 \frac{V^4}{(V+1)^2}.
\end{align}
For example, Fig.~\ref{fisher} plots the normalized $\mathcal G$
