\begin{lemma}
Let $(X,\|\cdot\|)$ be a Banach space. Then every Cauchy sequence in $X$ has a convergent subsequence.
\end{lemma}

This lemma is a well-known result in functional analysis and is used in the proof of Handelman's theorem. The proof of Handelman's theorem itself is a straightforward application of the monotone $\sigma$-completeness of $V$ and the properties of the norm on $V$.

