\begin{lemma}\label{lem:Eisnstn}
If $\Field{E}/\Field{F}$ is a ramified, quadratic extension, then $\oRing{\Field{E}}=\oRing{\Field{F}}[\varpi_{\Field{E}}]$ where $\varpi_{\Field{E}}$ is a root of an Eisenstein polynomial of the form,
$x^2+ax+b\varpi_{\Field{F}}$, where $b\in\mathrm{U}_{\Field{F}}$, and either $a=$ or $a\in\pIdeal{\Field{F}}^{v}\setminus\pIdeal{\Field{F}}^{v+1}$, with $2v=\val_\Field{E}(\diff{\varpi_{\Field{E}}})\leq\ramInd{\Field{F}}$.
\end{lemma}
\begin{proof}[Proof of \autoref{lem:Eisnstn}]
The ring of integers of $\Field{E}$ is generated by its local uniformizing parameter (l.u.p.) since $[\Field{E}:\Field{F}]=[\pIdeal{\Field{E}}:\pIdeal{\Field{F}}]=2$.

