\section*{Analysis of plasmonic properties of nanocomposite materials}

The plasmonic properties of the nanocomposite materials can be analyzed using various theoretical and experimental techniques. Here, we discuss some of the key aspects of this analysis.

\subsection{Thermal Analysis}
Thermal analysis is a fundamental technique for understanding the thermal behavior of nanocomposite materials. By measuring the temperature change of the material over time, one can determine the thermal conductivity, specific heat capacity, and other thermal properties. These properties are crucial for understanding how the nanocomposite material responds to thermal stimuli, such as heating or cooling.

\subsection{Electrical Analysis}
Electrical analysis is another important technique for studying the plasmonic properties of nanocomposite materials. This includes measuring the electrical conductivity, capacitance, and impedance of the material. These properties are essential for understanding the electronic and ionic transport within the nanocomposite.

\subsection{Optical Analysis}
