\section*{Walsh Function and Walsh Operators}
The discrete Walsh function $W_n$ is defined over the interval $[0,1)$ and is given by:
\begin{equation}
    W_n(x) = \sum_{j=0}^{N-1} (-1)^j \frac{x^j}{j!}
\end{equation}
where $x$ is a real number in the interval $[0,1)$.

Walsh operators $\hat{w}_i$ are defined as the conjugate transpose of the Walsh function $W_n$:
\begin{equation}
